<h2 class="sec">The moment</h2>
<div class="prose">
<p>Every real transition &mdash; a role you&rsquo;re growing into, a partnership finding its next shape, a life rearranging around a decision &mdash; has a space in the middle where the old way no longer fits and the new one hasn&rsquo;t formed yet. Most people cross it alone, or hand pieces of it to advisors who each see only their piece. That&rsquo;s where clarity and nerve quietly leak away.</p>
</div>

<hr class="rule" />

<section>
<h2 class="sec">How Triplicity helps</h2>
<p class="turn" style="margin-bottom:26px">You are not a problem to be solved. You are a whole to be held.</p>
<div class="coachcard">
<img src="/russ-michaels.jpg" alt="Russ Michaels, founder of Vault Human" width="120" height="150" />
<div><p class="coachname">Russ Michaels</p><p class="coachrole">Founder &middot; Vault Human</p></div>
</div>
<div class="prose">
<p>Triplicity is presence-led coaching and leadership development for people in transition. We don&rsquo;t optimize a role or fix a relationship from the outside &mdash; we hold the whole person and the whole situation, and work from there. What you leave with isn&rsquo;t a plan you were handed. It&rsquo;s your own judgment, clearer and steadier, walking out under its own power.</p>
</div>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<section id="begin">
<h2 class="sec">The Space Between</h2>
<div class="prose" style="margin-bottom:24px"><p>The signature engagement &mdash; a held, focused season of work through the transition that matters most.</p></div>
<ul class="steps">
<li><span class="rn">I</span><strong>A first conversation.</strong> Unhurried, no pitch &mdash; we find out together whether this is the room for the work.</li>
<li><span class="rn">II</span><strong>The work.</strong> A focused season together, in a rhythm that fits your life, holding the whole as it moves.</li>
<li><span class="rn">III</span><strong>You move whole.</strong> You leave with your own clarity and nerve &mdash; not a dependency, an integrity.</li>
</ul>
<div class="cta" style="margin-top:34px"><a class="btn-fill" href="#" data-open-form>Apply for a Conversation</a></div>
<p class="note">A short application &mdash; a few lines about where you are and what&rsquo;s shifting. If it&rsquo;s a fit, we start with an unhurried first conversation.</p>
</section>

